  "schema": "nfl2k5_board_kit/v1",
  "sources": [
    "SVG News, 30 July 2014, 'Cleveland Browns Revitalize In-Venue Video at FirstEnergy Stadium': 'The two main video displays will be nearly 40 ft. high and measure 192 ft. wide at the top, angling to 178 ft. wide in the middle and approximately 132 ft. wide along the bottom'; 'each new main end-zone display featuring a unique angled pattern on its north edge'; the new boards '32 ft. lower and 56 ft. closer to the field'.",
    "cleveland.com, June 2014 (archived): 'Two new video boards, nearly triple the size of the old units'; 'They are also 32 feet lower and 56 feet closer to the field'; Wikipedia, Huntington Bank Field: 'the upper level of the Dawg Pound was reduced to make way for a new, larger scoreboard'.",
    "The retail s30 scene (PROVED OFFLINE): the old boards' feed quads (group384) 31.7 x 9.7 m at y 37.5 to 47.3, z -136.1 (east, the Dawg Pound end: the cityscape puts the lake at -x, so -x is north and -z east) and +137.4 (west); their structures (group390, group389) to y 55; the clock and score digits on them.",
